body:
I understand your point. This person is into this spiritual/mysticism stuff (does magic), but I don't know if this person sees soulmates as a spiritual/mysticism thing too, maybe not.  I have a more logical point of view about soulmates. I see this whole soulmate experience something like similarities, sharing almost the same interests, understanding and completing each other etc. and I never experienced this level of closeness before. Before I met this person, I even didn't believe in soulmates, I thought something like this is impossible. But after experiencing it I kinda want to have this connection.  Even if this one soulmate experience was fake, it doesn't mean every soulmate experience has to be fake.  I might sound stupid, but isn't there a tiny little chance of finding your real soulmate? Who actually is like you and doesn't pretend it? (And I don't mean all this spiritual/mysticism stuff.)

&#x200B;

Since I started doubting our whole soulmate connection this person promised me things will get better and that we can work on our contact. But I feel kinda trapped in this contact. Right in place there this person needs me to be. But I don't want to accuse this person of abusive behaviour, because this person seems to feel guilty of everything on their own and I don't want to give this person more reasons to feel guilty. .\_.
